#
# Clause 4 of the symmetric CBD crossed with GRAPH SCOPE. `statements.ttl` is
# default-graph-only, so no case reading it can observe where a described
# statement LANDS — only that it was selected. This fixture is TriG for exactly
# that reason: every row it carries is asserted in a named graph, so an
# expectation written as N-Quads pins the graph of each reifier declaration and
# each annotation, not merely its presence.
#
# The rule these cases pin: a reifier DECLARATION is selected by its reified
# triple's subject-or-object membership in the closure and by nothing else —
# graph membership takes no part in the selection — and is then re-emitted into
# the graph that declared it. An annotation rides with the declaration it
# annotates, so it is harvested per `(reifier, graph)`.
@prefix :    <http://example.org/> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .

# Same-graph: the base quad, the reifier declaration and both annotations were
# all asserted in :g1, and describing :a must keep all four rows there.
GRAPH :g1 {
  :a :knows :b ~:r1 {| :certainty "high" ; :recordedBy :editor |} .
}

# Cross-graph: :g2 asserts the base quad, and :g3 — a DIFFERENT graph — declares
# a reifier about it and annotates that declaration. Graph-blind selection is
# what reaches the declaration at all; graph-faithful emission is what keeps it
# in :g3 rather than folding it beside the triple it reifies.
GRAPH :g2 {
  :p :mentions :q .
}

GRAPH :g3 {
  :r2 rdf:reifies <<( :p :mentions :q )>> .
  :r2 :source :ledger .
}

# Per-declaration annotation scope: ONE reifier id, :rs, declared in :g4 about a
# triple of :c and in :g5 about a triple of :m, each annotated with the SAME
# predicate in its own graph. Describing :c reaches only the :g4 declaration, so
# only the :g4 annotation may ride along — harvesting a reifier's rows across
# graphs would emit the :g5 annotation into a graph this description never
# declared :rs in.
GRAPH :g4 {
  :c :worksAt :acme ~:rs {| :since "2020" |} .
}

GRAPH :g5 {
  :m :knows :n ~:rs {| :since "1999" |} .
}
